<%# The face a persona wears, in the form that creates it and the one that
    edits it — the same partial in both, because a roster that differs between
    the two panels would let a persona be given a face it can never get back.

    The field is one button showing the face in use, not a grid of forty cells:
    a grid that large pushes the rest of the form off the panel, and the panel
    is the thing being read. Behind the button is a search across every emoji
    Unicode ships — far too much to send with the page, so it arrives as its
    own script the first time a picker is opened (see app.js), and the roster
    below is what the picker shows before that script lands.

    The cell that is picked writes the hidden field the form submits, and
    clears the free field beside it, so a click is never overruled by the echo
    of the face that was already there. The free field keeps the roster open:
    a face that is not in it is typed there and wins over any cell, which is
    the only way to say "none of those". On the edit form the field arrives
    already holding the current face when that face is off-roster; the channel
    treats a field still holding exactly that as unedited. Either answer is
    clipped to a single grapheme by the server, since the rail draws a face in
    a twenty-pixel circle.

    `selected` is the face already in use, `choices` the short roster that is
    shown first. -%>
<%
  face = selected.to_s
  listed = choices.include?(face)
-%>
<fieldset class="emoji-picker" data-emoji-picker data-emoji-recent="<%= h(choices.join(" ")) %>">
  <legend><%= h(I18n.t("web.emoji.label")) %></legend>
  <div class="emoji-head">
    <button type="button" class="emoji-face" data-emoji-toggle aria-expanded="false"
            aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.emoji.pick")) %>" title="<%= h(I18n.t("web.emoji.pick")) %>"><%= h(face) %></button>
    <input type="search" class="emoji-search" data-emoji-search placeholder="<%= h(I18n.t("web.emoji.search_placeholder")) %>"
           aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.emoji.search")) %>" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
  </div>
  <input type="hidden" name="emoji" value="<%= h(face) %>" data-emoji-input>
  <div class="emoji-panel" data-emoji-panel hidden>
    <div class="emoji-groups" data-emoji-groups></div>
    <div class="emoji-grid" data-emoji-grid></div>
    <p class="emoji-note" data-emoji-note></p>
  </div>
  <label class="emoji-other">
    <input type="text" name="emoji_custom" value="<%= listed ? "" : h(face) %>"
           maxlength="16" placeholder="<%= h(I18n.t("web.emoji.other_placeholder")) %>" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.emoji.other")) %>"
           autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
  </label>
</fieldset>
